## What Stone Pairs With Each Setting

Setting style affects which stone grade to prioritize.

**Solitaire settings:** Maximum stone visibility. Every flaw, every color tint, every proportion issue is exposed with nothing else to look at. Buy VS2 minimum clarity, G minimum color in white metal. Don't compromise on cut quality — Ideal cut only.

**Pavé settings:** The band sparkle creates competition for the eye. VS2 clarity is still right; you can sometimes drop to H color because the surrounding melee draws attention away from the corners. Save the color budget and put it toward carat weight.

**Hidden halo:** The halo sits below the table, so clarity is fully visible face-up. Stay at VS2 or above. Color: G in white metal, H in yellow/rose gold — same as solitaire.

**Bezel:** The metal rim hides the girdle and partially obscures the corners. You can be more flexible on clarity — VS2–SI1 in the table area works if you check that no inclusions fall near the corners. Color is more forgiving since the bezel itself creates a frame.

